// computation kernel
//
// Optimizations vs. original version:
//   * Removed the temporary z[ ] vector and the two passes that wrote z[ ]
//     and then copied it back to y[ ]. This reduces memory traffic and
//     improves cache behavior.
//   * Replaced the (z, y) update phase with an in-place update of y using
//     symmetric index pairs (i, j = k-i-1). Each pair is processed once,
//     using the original values y[i] and y[j], so the arithmetic is
//     identical to the original algorithm (no additional re-association).
//   * All data traversals still use Noarr traversers; only scalar operations
//     are done with plain C++ scalars.
